#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:80
msgid ""
"For compatibility, if ``~/.local/pipx`` exists (or ``~\\pipx`` on Windows), "
"pipx keeps using it. See the `platformdirs platform table <https://"
"platformdirs.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api.html#platforms>`_ for the resolved "
"directories. On Linux and macOS, ``platformdirs`` reads ``XDG_DATA_HOME`` "
"and ``XDG_CACHE_HOME``, so exporting either moves the matching pipx "
"directory; leave them unset for the platform default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:85
msgid ""
"These paths were introduced in 1.2.0 and temporarily reverted for macOS and "
"Windows between 1.5.0 and 1.16.0. To move an existing installation to the "
"new default, see :doc:`move-installation`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:90
msgid "Install for all users"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:92
msgid ""
"The ``--global`` flag installs into a system-wide location for all users. "
"Place it **after** the subcommand:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:94
msgid ""
"$ sudo pipx install --global pycowsay\n"
"$ sudo pipx list --global"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:99
msgid ""
"pipx silently ignores ``--global`` when it comes before the subcommand "
"(``sudo pipx --global install pycowsay``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:101
msgid ""
"Default global paths are ``/usr/local/bin`` for binaries, ``/usr/local/share/"
"man`` for man pages, and ``/opt/pipx`` for environments. Override them with "
"``PIPX_GLOBAL_BIN_DIR``, ``PIPX_GLOBAL_MAN_DIR``, and ``PIPX_GLOBAL_HOME``. "
"Add the global binary directory to the system ``PATH`` with ``sudo pipx "
"ensurepath --global``, which writes ``/etc/profile.d/pipx.sh`` on Linux and "
"``/etc/paths.d/pipx`` on macOS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:106
msgid ""
"You can also set the variables explicitly instead of using ``--global``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:108
msgid ""
"$ sudo PIPX_HOME=/opt/pipx PIPX_BIN_DIR=/usr/local/bin PIPX_MAN_DIR=/usr/"
"local/share/man pipx install <PACKAGE>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:114
msgid "``--global`` is not supported on Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:118
msgid "Prepend or preview the PATH edit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:120
msgid ""
"Pass ``--prepend`` to ``pipx ensurepath`` to prepend the pipx bin directory "
"to ``PATH`` instead of appending it, so pipx-installed binaries win over "
"system binaries of the same name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:123
msgid ""
"Pass ``--dry-run`` to report which directories ``ensurepath`` would add, "
"without touching ``PATH`` or any shell configuration file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:126
msgid "$ pipx ensurepath --dry-run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:132
msgid "Point pip at an index"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:134
msgid ""
"pipx uses pip internally for all installs, including its own shared "
"libraries. Set ``PIP_*`` environment variables to route pip at a private "
"index; pipx forwards them to every pip call. For per-command control use ``--"
"pip-args``. See :doc:`use-private-index` for the full recipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:138
msgid ""
"Set ``PIPX_DISABLE_SHARED_LIBS_AUTO_UPGRADE=1`` to skip automatic shared-"
"library upgrades during commands such as ``pipx install`` and ``pipx "
"upgrade``; ``pipx upgrade-shared`` still upgrades them. Use ``--skip-"
"maintenance`` to apply the same policy to one command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:142
msgid "$ pipx install --skip-maintenance my-package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:148
msgid "Verify it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:150
msgid ""
"$ pipx environment --value PIPX_HOME\n"
"$ pipx environment --value PIPX_BIN_DIR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/configure-paths.rst:155
msgid "Each prints the path pipx will use, reflecting any override you set."
msgstr ""
